    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        335.6746826171875,
        258.7783203125,
        354.4736022949219
      ],
      "text": "A. robots to explore outer space.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        75.12000274658203,
        355.59368896484375,
        383.57757568359375,
        414.1136169433594
      ],
      "text": "B. advances made in machine intelligence so far.\nC. changes made to other planets for our own benefit.\nD. the harm already done by artificial intelligence\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        427.0520324707031,
        509.8450927734375,
        465.8336181640625
      ],
      "text": "34. Richardson and Rees express similar views regarding the ethical aspect of\n__________.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        75.12000274658203,
        466.7710266113281,
        486.05499267578125,
        506.07244873046875
      ],
      "text": "35. Rees and Wolpert share an opinion about the extent of __________.\n36. Wolpert disagrees with Richardson on the question of __________.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        552.4520263671875,
        169.10899353027344,
        571.9534301757812
      ],
      "text": "Questions 37–40\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        586.2920532226562,
        289.9510498046875,
        605.79345703125
      ],
      "text": "Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        618.2110595703125,
        509.8582458496094,
        696.8336181640625
      ],
      "text": "37. What point does Richardson make about fear of machines?\nA. It has grown alongside the development of ever more advanced robots.\nB. It is the result of our inclination to attribute human characteristics to non-\nhuman entities.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        697.834716796875,
        504.2111511230469,
        736.43359375
      ],
